---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import HotelTaxMap from '../components/HotelTaxMap.astro';
import CompareByRegion from '../components/CompareByRegion.astro';
import USBadge from '../components/USBadge.astro';

// The hotel tax world map. A NEW PAGE rather than the hero of /hotel-taxes-and-fees, and
// the reasoning is worth keeping because it will come up again for the next map.
//
// The hub answers the query directly in its opening lines and already ranks on it. Putting
// a whole-world map above that copy pushes the answer below the fold, which is the exact
// failure RegionMap.astro's own note warns about ("so it sets the scene without pushing the
// answer below the fold"), and a world choropleth is far heavier than a locator inset. A
// page that exists to be screenshotted and linked also wants its own canonical URL to
// collect those links, rather than sending them to a hub whose job is the four-part
// explainer. So the hub keeps its opening and gains a prominent link down to here, and the
// map gets a URL of its own.
//
// The map does not try to rank as an island. Every shaded country links to its own hotel
// taxes spoke or its guide, which is where the sourced, dated detail lives and where the
// existing rankings are; the map is the discovery surface that feeds them.
//
// THE EMBED SNIPPET, and why it is a const rather than typed into the markup. The height has
// to agree with the real height of /embed/hotel-tax-map or the frame scrolls internally on a
// stranger's article, so it is a number somebody will need to retune when that page changes.
// Keeping it here, named, means it gets found. 720 is measured against the embed as built:
// the map is 1000 by 439, so at a typical 640px article column the figure is about 325px
// including its frame, and the head, colour scale, legend note and credit bar bring the whole
// thing to roughly 580px. The margin covers narrow columns, where the map shortens but the
// text wraps to more lines.
//
// loading=lazy so the embed costs the host page nothing until it scrolls near. The referrer
// policy is the browser default spelled out, so TTC can still see which sites are embedding
// the map without leaking a full URL to an http host.
const SNIPPET = `<iframe src="https://truetripcosts.com/embed/hotel-tax-map" width="100%" height="720"
  style="border:0" title="Hotel tax by country, from True Trip Costs" loading="lazy"
  referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"></iframe>`;
---
<Base
  title="Hotel tax by country, mapped: what governments add to a room rate"
  description="A world map of what government tax and mandatory levies add on top of a quoted hotel room rate, country by country. Government charges only, each one sourced and dated, with resort fees kept separate.">
  <Nav />
  <main class="wrap">

    <section class="htx-intro">
      <p class="lab">Hotel taxes and fees</p>
      <div style="margin:2px 0 12px"><USBadge /></div>
      <h1>The world, shaded by what gets added at checkout.</h1>
      <p class="htx-lede">Two hotel rooms can be advertised at the same price and settle hundreds of dollars apart, because what a government adds on top of a quoted rate ranges from nothing to roughly a quarter. This map colours countries by that gap alone: the tax and mandatory levies that appear after you have already compared prices.</p>
      <p class="htx-lede htx-lede2">It is a deliberately narrow question, and the narrowness is the point. A map of total tax burden would shade half of Europe dark and tell you nothing useful, because that tax is already inside the price you were quoted. What costs you a surprise is the part that is not, which is why some of the most heavily taxed countries in Europe sit at the light end here.</p>
    </section>

    <HotelTaxMap />

    <aside class="htx-embed-cta">
      <p class="htx-embed-cta-t">This map is free to embed, and it stays current on your page. As we check more countries and correct what changes, an embedded copy updates itself, no re-paste needed.</p>
      <a class="htx-embed-cta-b" href="#embed">Embed this map</a>
    </aside>

    <section class="htx-more">
      <h2>Where the detail lives</h2>
      <p>Each shaded country above links to its own write-up, which is where the rates are kept current, sourced against the authority that sets them and dated. For the four kinds of charge that land on a hotel bill and how to tell them apart, start with the <a href="/hotel-taxes-and-fees">hotel taxes and fees guide</a>. For per-night bed taxes and entry charges specifically, see <a href="/tourist-taxes">tourist taxes and fees</a>, and for what a day costs once the room is paid for, <a href="/cost-comparison">cost of a day, compared</a>.</p>
      <p class="htx-keep">Government rates are read off the tax authority, ministry or city that sets them and dated on the country's row. Service charges and resort fees are set by each property, so where we give a figure it is a range from recent reports rather than a published rate, and it never affects the shading. A country left unshaded has not been checked yet, which is not the same as a country with nothing to pay. More on how we work is on our <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="htx-embed" id="embed">
      <h2>Use this map on your own site</h2>
      <p>The map is free to embed anywhere, including commercially. It is served from here, so it stays current on your page as we check more countries and correct what changes. A credit link back is appreciated and not required: the frame carries one already.</p>

      <label class="htx-esnip-lab" for="htx-esnip">Paste this where you want the map</label>
      <textarea class="htx-esnip" id="htx-esnip" readonly rows="4" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="htx-ecopy-hint">{SNIPPET}</textarea>

      <div class="htx-erow">
        <button class="htx-ecopy" type="button" data-copy-snippet hidden>Copy the snippet</button>
        <span class="htx-ecopy-msg" data-copy-msg role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
        <a class="htx-eprev" href="/embed/hotel-tax-map" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See what it looks like</a>
      </div>
      <p class="htx-ehint" id="htx-ecopy-hint">Clicking the box selects the whole snippet, so it copies with one keystroke if the button is not there.</p>
    </section>

    <CompareByRegion />
  </main>
  <Footer />

  {/* The copy button is inline, dependency-free, and starts hidden. It is revealed by the
      script below only once the script has run and the clipboard API is actually present,
      so a reader with JavaScript off, or on a browser without it, never sees a button that
      does nothing. The snippet itself is a readonly textarea and selectable by hand either
      way, which is the path that always works. */}
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var box = document.getElementById('htx-esnip');
      var btn = document.querySelector('[data-copy-snippet]');
      var msg = document.querySelector('[data-copy-msg]');
      if (!box) return;

      // Clicking the box selects all of it. This is the no-button path and it is why the
      // button is allowed to be optional.
      box.addEventListener('focus', function () { box.select(); });
      box.addEventListener('click', function () { box.select(); });

      if (!btn || !navigator.clipboard || !navigator.clipboard.writeText) return;
      btn.hidden = false;

      var timer = null;
      btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        navigator.clipboard.writeText(box.value).then(function () {
          btn.textContent = 'Copied';
          if (msg) msg.textContent = 'Snippet copied to your clipboard.';
        }).catch(function () {
          // Do not claim success that did not happen. Fall back to selecting the text and
          // say so plainly.
          box.select();
          if (msg) msg.textContent = 'Could not copy automatically. The snippet is selected, so copy it now.';
        }).then(function () {
          clearTimeout(timer);
          timer = setTimeout(function () {
            btn.textContent = 'Copy the snippet';
            if (msg) msg.textContent = '';
          }, 2600);
        });
      });
    })();
  </script>

  <style>
    .htx-intro{max-width:720px;margin:22px 0 0}
    .htx-intro h1{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(26px,4.6vw,38px);letter-spacing:-.015em;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 12px}
    .htx-lede{font-size:18px;color:#3B4A46;line-height:1.55;margin:0}
    .htx-lede2{font-size:16px;color:var(--muted);margin:12px 0 0}
    .htx-more h2{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(21px,3.2vw,27px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 10px}
    .htx-more p{font-size:15px;color:#3B4A46;line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 12px;max-width:720px}
    .htx-more a{color:var(--teal-deep);font-weight:500;text-decoration:none}
    .htx-more a:hover{text-decoration:underline}
    .htx-keep{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:16px;margin-top:6px}

    /* The live-update promise, surfaced by the map rather than buried at the foot of the
       page, because "an embedded copy stays current" is the single strongest reason a site
       embeds this map instead of screenshotting it, and it was previously below the fold. */
    .htx-embed-cta{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;max-width:720px;margin:18px 0 0;padding:14px 16px;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:4px solid var(--teal);border-radius:10px}
    .htx-embed-cta-t{flex:1 1 320px;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.5;color:#3B4A46;margin:0}
    .htx-embed-cta-b{flex:none;font-family:var(--font);font-size:14px;font-weight:500;color:#F5F4EF;background:var(--teal-deep);border-radius:9px;padding:9px 16px;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap}
    .htx-embed-cta-b:hover{background:var(--teal)}
    /* Smooth scroll (and its reduced-motion opt-out) is already global in global.css; this
       only reserves a little breathing room above the target when the jump lands. */
    #embed{scroll-margin-top:16px}

    .htx-embed{max-width:720px;margin:34px 0 0;padding:22px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .htx-embed h2{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(21px,3.2vw,27px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 10px}
    .htx-embed p{font-size:15px;color:#3B4A46;line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 14px}
    .htx-esnip-lab{display:block;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:var(--teal-deep);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.09em;margin:0 0 7px}
    /* Monospace and pre-wrap, because this is code a reader is about to paste and a broken
       line in a proportional font is how a snippet arrives mangled. */
    .htx-esnip{width:100%;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--ink);background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:11px 12px;resize:vertical;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:break-word;-webkit-text-size-adjust:100%}
    .htx-esnip:focus{outline:2px solid var(--teal);outline-offset:1px}
    .htx-erow{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:10px 0 0}
    .htx-ecopy{font-family:var(--font);font-size:14px;font-weight:500;color:#F5F4EF;background:var(--teal-deep);border:0;border-radius:9px;padding:9px 15px;cursor:pointer}
    .htx-ecopy:hover{background:var(--teal)}
    .htx-ecopy-msg{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}
    .htx-eprev{font-size:14px;color:var(--teal-deep);font-weight:500;text-decoration:none}
    .htx-eprev:hover{text-decoration:underline}
    .htx-ehint{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin:10px 0 0}

    @media (max-width:560px){
      .htx-lede{font-size:16.5px}
      .htx-esnip{font-size:11.5px}
    }
  </style>
</Base>
